      "role": "user",
      "content": "Binary Search\n\nGiven a sorted (ascending) array of distinct integers nums and a target, return the index of target if it exists, otherwise -1. You must write an algorithm with O(log n) runtime.\n\nExample: nums = [-1,0,3,5,9,12], target = 9 -> 4.\nConstraints: 1 <= len(nums) <= 10^4.",
      "id": "m-0",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-02T01:17:50.651Z",
      "durationMs": 0
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "channel": "analysis",
      "content": "Complexity check: one pass, O(n) time, O(n) auxiliary space for the map. That meets the constraint.\n\nEdge cases to cover before submitting: empty input, single element, and the all-duplicates case.\n\nConstraints are small enough that the obvious approach fits, but the follow-up asks for the optimal one; going straight to it.",
      "id": "m-1",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-02T01:17:51.035Z",
      "durationMs": 5261,
      "stepIndex": 1
    },
